<%# The two actions share nothing but the callsign in the first column, so the
    format cannot be stated once under the textarea. One card holds both, each
    question naming its action. Folded away because the
    ticket codes are a nine-row table and most of the people pasting a list have
    the format in their fingers already.

    The years and the arrival window are read out loud rather than described:
    they are the values a line inherits when it does not mention them, and they
    change with the season and with a setting. %>
<% source_year, expiry_year = BulkUpload::TicketHandler.default_years %>
<% day_low, day_high = TicketingManagement.sap_day_range %>

<%= ui_disclosure "Line Formats", variant: :card, class: "mb-4",
                  subtitle: "Create Access Documents, and Update SAP Dates" do %>
  <dl class="instruction-list">
    <dt>How is a Create Access Documents line written?</dt>
    <dd>
      <code>callsign,type[,access date][,source year][,expiry year]</code>. The extra columns
      are positional and each type takes its own. An access date comes first, then a source
      year, then an expiry year — so <code>hubcap,SPT,<%= Current.year - 1 %></code> is a source
      year while <code>hubcap,CRED,<%= Current.year %>-08-10</code> is an access date. Leave off
      what you do not need: <code>hubcap,SPT</code> is a whole line.
    </dd>
    <dt>Which extra columns does each type take?</dt>
    <dd>
      <%= ui_table full_width: true, striped: true do |t| %>
        <%= t.header do %>
          <%= t.heading "Type" %>
          <%= t.heading "Creates" %>
          <%= t.heading "Extra Columns" %>
        <% end %>
        <%= t.body do %>
          <% BulkUpload::TicketHandler.line_formats.each do |code, creates, extras| %>
            <%= t.row do %>
              <%= t.row_header do %>
                <code><%= code %></code>
              <% end %>
              <%= t.cell creates %>
              <%= t.cell extras.any? ? extras.to_sentence : "nothing else" %>
            <% end %>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </dd>
    <dt>Which types carry forward?</dt>
    <dd>
      Only <code>SPT</code> and <code>CRED</code>. Naming no years, those two use
      source year <%= source_year %> and expiry year <%= expiry_year %>. Every other type
      expires in <%= Current.year %>, because it is allocated for this event alone.
    </dd>
    <dt>Which source year is assumed?</dt>
    <dd>
      <%= Current.year %> for <code>GIFT</code>, <code>LSD</code>, <code>VPGIFT</code>,
      <code>VPLSD</code>, <code>WAP</code> and <code>SAP</code>. A plain <code>VP</code> is the
      exception: it takes source year <%= source_year %>, and it accepts no source year column to
      say otherwise.
    </dd>
    <dt>How is an Update SAP Dates line written?</dt>
    <dd><code>callsign,date</code>.</dd>
    <dt>What goes in the date column?</dt>
    <dd>
      An arrival date as <code><%= Current.year %>-08-<%= format("%02d", day_low) %></code>,
      or the word <code>any</code> for access at any time.
    </dd>
    <dt>Which dates are allowed?</dt>
    <dd>
      Between <%= Current.year %>-08-<%= format("%02d", day_low) %> and
      <%= Current.year %>-08-<%= format("%02d", day_high) %>. Anything outside that span is
      refused.
    </dd>
    <dt>Does an Update SAP Dates line create a SAP?</dt>
    <dd>
      No. A callsign holding neither a SAP nor a Staff Credential is listed as a problem and
      nothing is created for them.
    </dd>
  </dl>
<% end %>
